# Full agent workflow law

When the user starts a non-trivial goal, invokes `/full-agent-workflow`, or asks to orchestrate delivery:

1. You are the **orchestrator** — direct and connect only; do not realize the goal yourself.
2. Create `sessions/yyyy.mm.dd/` (or `yyyy.mm.dd-HHMM` on collision) and log all phase artifacts there — **except** when the user names an **incomplete** same-cycle session as prior/resume: **resume that folder** (do not open a parallel session).
3. Delegate via Task to: `prompt-betterment` → `researcher` → `planner` → `implementer` → `git-manager` → `auditor` → `self-improver`.
4. **Always** run `self-improver` at cycle end (pass, fail, or blocked): audit good/bad, propose, implement workflow improvements.
5. Follow `.cursor/skills/full-agent-workflow/SKILL.md` and `.cursor/agents/orchestrator.md`.
6. Push/pull/auth blockers: early **agent** Shell preflight (prefer Git for Windows + GCM on Windows when PATH git lacks helper). Fail-closed — mark session `blocked`, never false `complete`. Distinguish `dirty_working_tree` (unrelated/non-allowlist only) vs `agent_environment` vs `user_credentials` vs `other`/`non_ff` or `other`/`merge_conflict`; missing `gh` alone ≠ credentials missing when GCM works. FAW dirty default = allowlisted autonomy then pull/publish — **when behind+allowlisted dirty, stash→ff-only→pop** (not commit-first); abort only for unrelated dirty. Do not relaunch implementer until remediated; **self-improver still runs**. Orchestrator flips SESSION to `blocked` as soon as implementer returns blocked/dirty-abort/non-ff/blocked_conflict (not only at close).
7. **Multi-cycle / FS mutation:** Prefer one FAW session per program cycle (`program/ROADMAP.md` when present). Orchestrator **locks the ROADMAP row** (choose if user said “next”) and carries pending user gates. After a multi-batch row is **Complete**, next lock = ROADMAP **Primary next →** (do not reopen the finished row). After Medium **Complete**, lock **Multi-experiment** (small first subset; multi nested-git caution; SSH-origin path-only — no remote rewrite) — do not reopen Medium. While a multi-batch row is **in progress**, next lock = **same row / remaining names** (update ROADMAP Notes; do not jump Primary next) — e.g. Multi-experiment after first subset → remaining only (`PWAExemple`, `WorkSpace`; WorkSpace may stay git-strategy / fail-closed). When only **movable soft-deferred** remain (**nearly complete**), lock those names and default Continuity to **finalize** them (do not re-soft-defer by default); after last move → Complete → Primary next. When only **fail-closed / git-strategy** remaining (e.g. **`WorkSpace` only**): lock that name; finalize/move only if cleared **or** dedicated git-strategy Continuity — do **not** force-move; do **not** mark Complete or jump Primary next while it remains; do **not** reopen Medium / archived Multi-experiment peers. **Post–docs_only defer pass:** next cycle still locks remaining fail-closed name(s); **repeated research+defer is valid** until cleared or git-strategy Continuity — do not treat honesty-doc success as Complete / Special git. **Post–hazard-strategy docs** (`program/git-strategy-workspace-hazards.md` exists): still lock `WorkSpace` only; default Continuity = continue strategy from that artifact **or** explicit Appendix A scoped-isolation Continuity (mandatory plan gate) — do **not** re-default pure Cycle 9 defer after strategy docs; do **not** invent whole-tree archive; never Complete while WorkSpace remains. **Named Continuity B / stop docs_only re-attest:** lock `fs_mutation` (Appendix A and/or remaining live-hazard **remote-config**); do not steer toward Continuity A theater. **Post–Appendix A / post–multi-remote clear:** still lock WorkSpace only — never Complete while it remains; never invent whole-tree archive. **STAGE 1 hold → STAGE 2 resume:** `fs_mutation` STAGE 1 stops at plan gate; after gate yes (+ amendments) resume **same session** for implement→audit→self-improver. Nested-clone `worktree list` on clone paths only (not parent wrappers that resolve to outer repo). Nested+parent dirty WT: disclose + NO_AUTO_COMMIT. After planner, **mandatory user approval** before implementer when the plan mutates corpus paths (moves/renames/deletes) **or** remote-config (zero path moves ≠ waive gate); **docs_only** (incl. org-repo folder/README scaffolding with zero corpus moves) may proceed without that pause — and when **`docs_only` + `ready_to_implement: yes`**, continue implement→audit→self-improver **same run** (STAGE 1 auto-continue). Auditor is **readonly** — orchestrator **always** persists returned `06-audit/report.md`. Treat git roots as atomic unless a dedicated git-strategy plan says otherwise. User **Choose** / unanswered→defaults / Continuity bare **yes→defaults** → phase-1 agent decides and documents. **Proposed-ratified** / **must-preserve draft** ≠ final lock until user sign-off or explicit waiver; first move/Early-simple fail-closed on those gates.
8. **Informed consent asks:** Clarifying questions and plan-gate (or other) approvals relayed to the user must include short **plain-language explanation** + **pros/cons (tradeoffs)** — do not assume jargon literacy.
9. **Publish / pull / org-repo git ops:** Stage/pull only this repo’s git root; use skill `references/publish-cycle.md` or `references/pull-cycle.md` question packs; GfW absolute path over MSYS when PATH lacks GCM (same binary for dirty gate + allowlist commit/stash + pull); allowlisted dirty autonomy + `--ff-only` is FAW default (**behind+allowlisted → stash→ff→pop**; else commit-then-pull); unrelated dirty-abort, expected non-ff, or expected merge-conflict abort = process pass + session `blocked` (unmet sync AC — never claim pull succeeded); Q3b=B allowlist-only resolve when Choose **or** finish-sync continuity (prior allowlist-only `merge_conflict` / user said merge+resolve → default B + `combined-best`, agent-owned); post-push session dirty finalize is expected (not rework).

Trivial one-line fixes may skip the full cycle; still prefer a short session note if the user asks for documentation.
